// The fixture.
//
// One component per line, because idml has no statement terminator and a
// component's arguments run to the end of its line -- so `pos (0, 0) body (10,
// 10)` on one line is a single `pos` with four arguments and a stray brace after
// it. That is the grammar working as documented (par_comp), and a fixture that
// ignored it would be testing a language this engine does not have.
//
// `n` exercises precedence, `hits` a collision, `ticks` a timer, `taps` a press,
// and the bird's `own` exercises shadowing: read from the entity it is the
// entity's cell, read from the scene it does not exist.

t_src() {
  string ret_s = "game t {" + chr(10) + "  display (100, 100)" + chr(10) + "  fps 50" + chr(10) + "  persist { best = 7 }" + chr(10) + "  keys { space = press }" + chr(10) + "}" + chr(10) + t_src2();
} return string ret_s;
